# The arguments of the receivers call and fncall are named and are given by position or by name through `:=` (the
# author 2026-11-11, LMX_blog/2026-11-11.md#structure-call-by-name; R22, item 4; plan M11 5b): one binder for every
# receiver, at the root and in a callable's code; the operands are evaluated in the order they are written.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root keeps its launches over
# the paths main\data\Name, holds the places and calls main().
# The root launches stand before main(): they run over the data of main before its code does, as the original ran
# them before inside(); the order fixes the values 12, 12, 17 and 13.
sub: main () (
    Args:
        int: a 5
    Vars:
        int: x 10
    Bump:
        x := x + 1
    Read:
        return: x
    Add:
        return: x + a
    int: in_method 0
)
    fn: inside () int
        call(code := Bump; data := Vars)
        return: fncall(return := int; code := Read; data := Vars)
    in_method := inside()
call(data := main\data\Vars; code := main\data\Bump)
call(code := main\data\Bump; data := main\data\Vars)
int: named fncall(data := main\data\Vars; return := int; code := main\data\Read)
int: mixed fncall(main\data\Vars; code := main\data\Read; return := int)
int: with_args fncall(args := main\data\Args; data := main\data\Vars; return := int; code := main\data\Add)
main()
int: in_method main\data\in_method
int: vars_x main\data\Vars\x
